artifact.self_contained_problem:
Consider a right triangle with legs of length x and y, hypotenuse z, and altitude u drawn from the right angle perpendicular to the hypotenuse. Inscribe inside this triangle a square of side length v whose one side lies on the hypotenuse (so that v = uz/(u+z)). All five quantities x, y, z, u, v are measured in the unit "sun"; areas are measured in "square bu" (1 square bu equals 1 square sun), and lengths in the relation below use the conversion 1 shaku = 10 sun.

Suppose that:
(i) the area of the triangle outside the inscribed square equals 350 square bu, i.e. (1/2)xy − v² = 350;
(ii) five sevenths of the leg y plus two thirds of the altitude u equals 4 shaku 5 sun, i.e. (5/7)y + (2/3)u = 45;
(iii) the Pythagorean relation x² + y² = z² holds;
(iv) the altitude-on-hypotenuse relation xy = uz holds.

Determine the values of x, y, z, u, and v.

